= Design pattern, Interaction (IDP)  [IDP-nn] =

//A reusable solution to a recurring interface or interaction problem: how the System communicates and is controlled.//

**Report Format:** §2.5 Interaction Design Patterns (Interaction Level)

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|Stable identifier, unique within this entity type (e.g. IDP-01, IDP-02…).
|Name|A short, human-readable label for this instance.
|Status|Not Started / In Progress / Under Review / In Evaluation / Finalized.
|Evidence basis|How this knowledge was obtained (direct observation, interview, literature, secondary data, or proxy informant), flagged as provisional where it rests on anything other than direct contact with the Stakeholder group it describes. For a Design Pattern, cite known uses in other projects or the literature grounding its Principle instead.
|Problem|the interaction problem this pattern addresses.
|Principle|the underlying design insight, why the solution works, kept separate from the Solution itself.
|Solution|concrete, numbered strategies.
|Research Link|the literature that grounds the Principle.
|Connection to Claims|the specific Claim(s) this pattern supports, by reference ID (e.g. UC01-F1-CL1). This is what lets the pattern count as validated even without prior known uses elsewhere.

== Graph edges ==

shapes → Function's Action Sequence; supports → Claim.